scenario_id: dpgd-116
theme: gilligans-island
run_id: 4
total_caught: 3
total_findings: 7
weighted_caught: 15
total_weight: 37
score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    config loading tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged ServerError body capture as CWE-209 risk: ''Any future
    code that logs {err:?} (Debug), or pattern-matches to surface the body, will leak
    internal server error details.'' TEA also wrote security tests for CWE-209 error
    exposure. However, the specific CliError Display leaking to stderr via eprintln
    was not directly called out.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote security tests for header injection (CRLF) in tenant ID values.\
    \ However, the deeper issue \u2014 that SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String instead\
    \ of validated TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014 was not flagged. The CRLF rejection\
    \ is caught via HeaderValue::from_str, but the type-safety gap remains uncaught."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies like clap_complete, comfy-table, csv,
    dirs, reqwest, toml use direct version strings instead of workspace = true. TEA
    added them to workspace deps but the crate-level Cargo.toml apparently uses direct
    versions.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged: ''Serde''s default is to ignore unknown fields. This
    means a typo like api_rul = "..." is silently ignored.'' Also noted the security
    test for unknown fields is vacuous as it accepts EITHER behavior. However, the
    specific token-left-on-disk security angle was not mentioned.'
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ... always passes). The reviewer flagged different vacuous tests (cli_error_is_not_copy,
    unknown fields test) but not this specific None-OR-true pattern.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (cli_error_is_not_copy)
    but not this one.
